+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers, so the model knows the shape of a call. Nothing checked that the call it actually sent matched. This spec states what the registry enforces between the two: a call the schema rejects fails in one predictable way, returned as a tool result the model can read and correct inside the existing tool-round budget, and a call the schema accepts reaches the executor exactly as it arrived.
+
+## The contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema`
+  before the executor runs
+  ([validated by: returns a rejection naming what the schema rejected and skips the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L69),
+  [validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so the next round can correct it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L179)).
+- A call the schema rejects is returned as a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure,
+  rather than thrown
+  ([validated by: returns a rejection naming what the schema rejected and skips the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L69),
+  [validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so the next round can correct it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L179)).
+- The executor is never invoked for input the schema rejects
+  ([validated by: returns a rejection naming what the schema rejected and skips the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L69),
+  [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, redacting the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+- Validation enforces the schema's `required` list, declared property types and `enum` values, and
+  nothing beyond them
+  ([validated by: returns a rejection naming what the schema rejected and skips the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L69),
+  [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, redacting the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108),
+  [validated by: passes accepted input to the executor unchanged, extra properties included](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
+- A rejection message names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and carries no
+  property value
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, redacting the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+- No log line written while a rejected call is handled carries an input value
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, redacting the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged -- unlisted properties included, nothing
+  injected or coerced
+  ([validated by: passes accepted input to the executor unchanged, extra properties included](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register`, so a schema that cannot compile fails at
+  registration with an error naming the tool
+  ([validated by: throws at register when the input schema cannot compile, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L131),
+  [validated by: keeps validating a static tool against the schema it was registered with](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L154)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved per call and validated against the schema
+  current at that call
+  ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L138)).
+- A rejected tool call reaches the provider as a tool result on the next round, so `processMessage`
+  resolves and the model can correct the call within the tool-round budget
+  ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so the next round can correct it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L179)).
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name
+  ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for a name that was never registered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L171)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- There is no opt-out flag: every registered tool is validated, and no per-tool or per-call switch
+  turns it off.
+- An unregistered name keeps its existing `Unknown tool: <name>` throw -- the same failure class
+  handled the opposite way, an intentional split tracked separately.
+- Validating tool _output_, hallucination detection and an evaluation harness, per-tool
+  authorization (a schema-valid call for someone else's data is still valid), and retry, timeout
+  and rate limiting around tool execution are separate concerns.
